# Keep LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# This is load-bearing, not cosmetic. data/generate.py writes seed.sql with an
# explicit newline="\n", and `python data/generate.py --check` compares the
# committed file against freshly generated output BYTE FOR BYTE. With git's
# default autocrlf on Windows, a fresh clone would check seed.sql out with CRLF
# and the determinism check would fail for every Windows teammate -- on a file
# nobody had touched.
#
# The whole baseline-vs-harness comparison rests on that file being identical
# everywhere, so pin the line endings rather than trusting per-machine config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated dump: never convert, never diff it in review.
data/seed.sql -text linguist-generated=true

# PowerShell is happiest with CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

*.gguf binary
